{"type":"app","meta":{"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/editorial-policy/layout,_N_T_/editorial-policy/page,_N_T_/editorial-policy"},"segmentPaths":["/_tree","/_full","/editorial-policy/__PAGE__","/editorial-policy","/_index","/_head"]},"html":"<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charSet=\"utf-8\"/><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"/><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/_next/static/chunks/0_novvjei_gxi.css\" data-precedence=\"next\"/><link rel=\"preload\" as=\"script\" fetchPriority=\"low\" href=\"/_next/static/chunks/0wa60lc2wlwoc.js\"/><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/15orcrkp-_9ct.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/2ncdmtj91g36a.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/166-a3utgd-lq.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/turbopack-10b5wutro9flo.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/3i2zmhpv5m7u2.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\" async=\"\"></script><script async=\"\" src=\"https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-6710458178434465\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script><link rel=\"preload\" href=\"https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-C9HPD23Y02\" as=\"script\"/><link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/manifest.json\"/><title>Editorial Policy — BestAnimalNames.com | How We Create Name Content</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Learn how BestAnimalNames.com curates animal names, researches blog content, and maintains accuracy. Our editorial team follows rigorous standards for every page.\"/><link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/manifest.json\"/><meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"animal names, pet name generator, dog names, cat names, male names, female names, cute names\"/><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\"/><meta name=\"p:domain_verify\" content=\"acc18c9aa2855ead49c874b6cac9cb61\"/><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://bestanimalnames.com/editorial-policy/\"/><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Editorial Policy — BestAnimalNames.com\"/><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Our editorial standards: how we research, curate, and maintain every animal name and blog article.\"/><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\"/><meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Editorial Policy — BestAnimalNames.com\"/><meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"How we research and curate every animal name.\"/><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com\",\"description\":\"Free animal name generator with 989+ animals. Browse thousands of name ideas across 9 categories.\",\"potentialAction\":{\"@type\":\"SearchAction\",\"target\":{\"@type\":\"EntryPoint\",\"urlTemplate\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/animals?q={search_term_string}\"},\"query-input\":\"required name=search_term_string\"}}</script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/0cz1d0mv5g_q7.js\" noModule=\"\"></script></head><body class=\"min-h-screen flex flex-col bg-[#f8fafc] text-[#1e293b]\"><div hidden=\"\"><!--$--><!--/$--></div><header class=\"bg-white border-b border-gray-200 sticky top-0 z-50\"><nav class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 h-16 flex items-center justify-between\" aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a class=\"text-xl font-bold text-primary hover:text-primary-dark transition-colors\" href=\"/\">🐾 AnimalNameGen</a><div class=\"flex gap-6 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600\"><a class=\"hover:text-primary transition-colors\" href=\"/animals/\">Animals</a><a class=\"hover:text-primary transition-colors\" href=\"/guide/japanese-animal-names/\">Guides</a><a class=\"hover:text-primary transition-colors\" href=\"/blog/\">Blog</a></div></nav></header><main class=\"flex-1\" aria-label=\"Main content\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Editorial Policy\",\"item\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/editorial-policy/\"}]}</script><nav class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-500 flex gap-1 flex-wrap\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a class=\"hover:text-primary\" href=\"/\">Home</a><span class=\"text-gray-300\">/</span><span class=\"text-gray-800 font-medium\">Editorial Policy</span></nav><section class=\"bg-gradient-to-br from-primary to-indigo-700 text-white\"><div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-14 text-center\"><h1 class=\"text-4xl font-extrabold mb-4\">📋 Editorial Policy</h1><p class=\"text-indigo-100 text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto\">How we research, curate, and maintain every animal name and article on BestAnimalNames.com.</p></div></section><section class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 space-y-10 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\"><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-400\">Last updated: June 24, 2026</p><div><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Our Mission</h2><p>BestAnimalNames.com exists to help people find the perfect name for their animal companion. We believe naming an animal should be joyful, not frustrating. Our goal is to provide well-researched, genuinely useful naming resources — free of charge, forever.</p><p class=\"mt-3\">We are not a generic name generator that spits out random combinations. We are an editorial resource. Every name, every article, and every recommendation on this site passes through human review before publication.</p></div><div><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">How We Curate Animal Names</h2><p>Each animal page on BestAnimalNames.com contains name suggestions organized into categories: male, female, cute, funny, cool, unique, baby, and fantasy. Here is exactly how those names are selected:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2\"><li><strong>Research Sources</strong> — We draw from pet owner communities, veterinary naming surveys, zoological databases, cultural naming traditions, mythology references, and real-world naming trends reported by animal shelters and breeders.</li><li><strong>Human Review</strong> — Every candidate name is evaluated by our editorial team against clear quality criteria: ease of pronunciation, positive associations, distinctiveness, and suitability for the specific animal species.</li><li><strong>Category Assignment</strong> — Names are sorted into categories based on their tone and typical usage context. A name like “Thor” belongs in Cool or Fantasy categories, while “Marshmallow” fits Cute or Funny.</li><li><strong>Species Relevance</strong> — We never copy-paste the same list across different animals. Names for a horse should reflect equine characteristics, while names for a hamster should suit a small, gentle companion.</li><li><strong>Regular Refreshing</strong> — Collections are updated regularly as new naming trends emerge, pop culture introduces new references, and readers submit suggestions.</li></ul></div><div><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">How We Write Blog Articles</h2><p>Our blog covers animal naming guides, pet care naming tips, breed-specific advice, cultural naming traditions, and creative naming inspiration. Every article follows this process:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2\"><li><strong>Topic Selection</strong> — We choose topics that real pet owners and animal lovers are actually searching for, based on keyword research, reader requests, and gaps in existing online resources.</li><li><strong>Research &amp; Fact-Checking</strong> — Writers consult veterinary publications, ethology research, breed standards from kennel clubs, zoological references, and cultural naming guides. Every factual claim is verified before publication.</li><li><strong>Drafting</strong> — Articles are written by experienced writers with genuine knowledge of the subject. We do not publish AI-only content without human review.</li><li><strong>Editorial Review</strong> — Each draft goes through an editorial check for accuracy, readability, completeness, and adherence to our quality standards.</li><li><strong>Publishing &amp; Updates</strong> — Once published, articles are periodically reviewed and updated to reflect new research, naming trends, and reader feedback.</li></ul></div><div><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Quality Standards</h2><p>Every piece of content on BestAnimalNames.com must meet these baseline requirements:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2\"><li><strong>Accuracy</strong> — Animal facts and naming information must be verifiable from reputable sources.</li><li><strong>Completeness</strong> — Each animal page must include all eight name categories with at least 20 suggestions per category.</li><li><strong>Originality</strong> — We do not scrape or duplicate content from other websites. Every page is original.</li><li><strong>Accessibility</strong> — Content is organized with clear headings, readable fonts, high-contrast design, and proper ARIA labels for screen readers.</li><li><strong>Transparency</strong> — We clearly distinguish editorial content from advertisements. No sponsored content is published without disclosure.</li></ul></div><div><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Corrections &amp; Feedback</h2><p>We are committed to accuracy and continuous improvement. If you find an error, outdated information, or a name suggestion you believe is inappropriate, please let us know immediately:</p><p class=\"mt-3\">📧 <strong>Email:</strong> <a class=\"text-primary hover:underline\" href=\"mailto:support@bestanimalnames.com\">support@bestanimalnames.com</a></p><p class=\"mt-1\">📝 <strong>Contact Form:</strong> <a class=\"text-primary hover:underline\" href=\"/contact/\">Contact Us page</a></p><p class=\"mt-3\">We review all reports within 48 hours on weekdays and correct verified errors promptly. Corrections are noted with the date of revision.</p></div><div><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Independence &amp; Funding</h2><p>BestAnimalNames.com is an independent project, not owned by any corporation or venture capital firm. We fund our operations through non-intrusive advertising (Google AdSense). Advertisements are always clearly distinguishable from editorial content, and advertisers have zero influence over our naming recommendations or article content.</p></div><div class=\"bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-6 mt-8\"><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-blue-900 mb-2\">📖 Related Pages</h3><ul class=\"space-y-1 text-sm\"><li><a class=\"text-blue-700 hover:underline\" href=\"/about/\">About BestAnimalNames.com</a> — Our story and mission</li><li><a class=\"text-blue-700 hover:underline\" href=\"/how-we-create-content/\">How We Create Content</a> — Behind-the-scenes process</li><li><a class=\"text-blue-700 hover:underline\" href=\"/contact/\">Contact Us</a> — Submit feedback or report an error</li></ul></div></section><!--$--><!--/$--></main><footer class=\"bg-gray-900 text-gray-400 py-10\" aria-label=\"Site footer\"><div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-8\"><div><h4 class=\"text-white font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-wide mb-3\">Company</h4><ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm\"><li><a class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/about/\">About</a></li><li><a class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/editorial-policy/\">Editorial Policy</a></li><li><a class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/how-we-create-content/\">How We Create Content</a></li><li><a class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/contact/\">Contact</a></li><li><a class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/faq/\">FAQ</a></li></ul></div><div><h4 class=\"text-white font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-wide mb-3\">Legal</h4><ul class=\"s