ogy references, and real-world naming trends reported by animal shelters and breeders.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Human Review\"}],\" — Every candidate name is evaluated by our editorial team against clear quality criteria: ease of pronunciation, positive associations, distinctiveness, and suitability for the specific animal species.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Category Assignment\"}],\" — Names are sorted into categories based on their tone and typical usage context. A name like “Thor” belongs in Cool or Fantasy categories, while “Marshmallow” fits Cute or Funny.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Species Relevance\"}],\" — We never copy-paste the same list across different animals. Names for a horse should reflect equine characteristics, while names for a hamster should suit a small, gentle companion.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Regular Refreshing\"}],\" — Collections are updated regularly as new naming trends emerge, pop culture introduces new references, and readers submit suggestions.\"]}]]}]]}],\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\",\"$L15\",\"$L16\"]}]],null,\"$L17\"]}]\n18:[]\ne:\"$W18\"\nf:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{\"children\":\"$L1a\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L1b\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1c\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$L1d\"}]}]}],null]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0_novvjei_gxi.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n1e:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/3i2zmhpv5m7u2.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\"],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n12:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\",\"children\":\"How We Write Bl